<h2>Object class</h2>

<p>With the ```Object``` class, we can create instances of different classes (polymorphism), but to use the methods of these classes, we have to use downcasting (as shown in the example below). <b>All classes in Java inherit from the</b> ```Object``` <b>class directly or indirectly</b>.</p>

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Object x = new Coordinates(2, 3);
        System.out.println(((Coordinates)x).getX());
        System.out.println(x.getClass()); // getting the name of the class the object belongs to
    }
}

class Coordinates {
