<h2><a id="stringbuilder-class">The <code style={{color: "#157267"}}>StringBuilder</code> class</a></h2>
<p>The ```StringBuilder``` class is used for creating and modifying mutable strings. Unlike ```String```, which creates a new object on every modification, it allows for more efficient string manipulation.</p>

```java
import java.lang.StringBuilder;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("Hello");
        
        // Appending to the string
        sb.append(" World!");
        System.out.println(sb); // "Hello World!"
        
        // Inserting into the string
        sb.insert(5, ",");
        System.out.println(sb); // "Hello, World!"
        
        // Reversing the string
        sb.reverse();
        System.out.println(sb); // "!dlrow ,olleH"
    }
}
```

