<h2><a id="writing-to-a-file">Writing to a file</a></h2>

<p>The ```file_put_contents()``` method is used to write data to a file. If the file does not exist, it will be created. We can also use this method to overwrite existing files or append data based on the optional flags provided. Writing to a file: ```file_put_contents($file_name, $content);```. Appending to a file: ```file_put_contents($file_name, $content, FILE_APPEND);```. The ```file_get_contents()``` method is used to read from a file (```$content = file_get_contents($file_name);```).</p>
